# fleet

## Intent
Own the Pi-free Effect service contracts and subprocess adapters consumed by the fleet extension.

## Contract
`FleetGitService` provides branch, dirty, ahead/behind, sync-plan, and explicit hard-sync operations. `FleetGitLabService` reads open merge requests. `FleetPackageService` reads named package versions and runs frozen installs. `FleetPortlessService` discovers and removes only servers classified as orphaned. `FleetConfirmationService` is supplied at the Pi boundary for destructive confirmation. Service failures are represented by `FleetServiceError`; repository-selection failures use `FleetRepositoryError` in the extension policy.

## Behaviour
All services are injected into the extension core and remain independently fakeable. Every Git command runs with the selected repository path as its working directory, and ahead/behind resolves that repository's `origin/HEAD` with `origin/main` and `origin/master` fallbacks. The live layer runs Git, GitLab, pnpm, and portless subprocesses, decodes their structured results, and maps failures to typed `FleetServiceError` values. Open-MR lookup uses `glab mr list --source-branch ... --output json` because the installed CLI defaults to open merge requests and does not support `--state`. Portless orphan discovery skips running servers and existing worktree paths.

## Edge cases
- Missing or malformed subprocess output and nonzero exits become actionable `FleetServiceError` values that retain the failed command output.
- All branch, dirty-state, and range commands execute in the selected repository rather than the harness session checkout.
- Repositories whose default branch is `master` use `origin/master`; `main` is never assumed globally.
- Open-MR lookup never passes unsupported `--state` syntax to `glab mr list`.
- A package absent from all supported dependency scopes is returned with an undefined version.
- Running portless servers and servers whose declared worktree path exists are not classified as orphans.

## Non-goals
This library does not select repositories, register Pi tools, infer repository matrices, or decide whether a hard sync is allowed.

## Evidence
The fleet extension core tests inject fake Git, GitLab, package, portless, and confirmation services to exercise the service contracts across status, versions, sync, install, and prune actions.

